# 623. Add One Row to Tree

**Problem Link:** [LeetCode - Add One Row to Tree](https://leetcode.com/problems/add-one-row-to-tree/)

## Approach: Recursive DFS

1. If the required depth is `1`, create a new root node with the given value and attach the original tree as its left child.
2. Otherwise, use recursive DFS to traverse the tree.
3. When `curr_depth == depth - 1`, insert two new nodes:
   - Attach the new node as the left child and connect its left pointer to the original left subtree.
   - Attach the new node as the right child and connect its right pointer to the original right subtree.
4. Continue the recursion until the required depth is reached.

## Code (C++)

```cpp
class Solution {
public:

    void solve(TreeNode* root, int val, int depth, int curr_depth) {
        if (!root) return;

        if (curr_depth == depth) {
            TreeNode* node1 = new TreeNode(val);
            TreeNode* node2 = new TreeNode(val);

            TreeNode* l = root->left;
            TreeNode* r = root->right;

            root->left = node1;
            root->right = node2;

            if (l) node1->left = l;
            if (r) node2->right = r;
        }

        solve(root->left, val, depth, curr_depth + 1);
        solve(root->right, val, depth, curr_depth + 1);
    }

    TreeNode* addOneRow(TreeNode* root, int val, int depth) {
        if (depth == 1) {
            TreeNode* node = new TreeNode(val);
            node->left = root;
            return node;
        }

        solve(root, val, depth - 1, 1);
        return root;
    }
};
```

## Complexity Analysis

- **Time Complexity:** O(N) — In the worst case, we visit every node in the tree.
- **Space Complexity:** O(H) — Recursive call stack, where H is the height of the tree.
